    oe:aboutDisease oed:acute_kidney_injury ;
    oe:answerText "Most sepsis patients develop sepsis-associated acute kidney injury (SA-AKI), which poses a significant threat to survival and lacks specific treatment. To date, there are no published randomized controlled trials that have established a link between albumin use and SA-AKI development in sepsis."^^xsd:string ;
